0..76 Comment "// The pure λ-calculus as data and its single substitution, the base of the"
77..151 Comment "// λ-calculus syntax model (#640). `theory LC` is the single-substitution"
152..229 Comment "// calculus of Kaposi and Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_,"
230..299 Comment "// FSCD 2024, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10, §7): the presentation"
300..374 Comment "// `first_order` mints from `theory Lambda`, its names written without the"
375..447 Comment "// generated `$` and its context arguments implicit, as a `theory` block"
448..523 Comment "// writes them (#2422). The syntax model\'s carriers are de Bruijn terms and"
524..599 Comment "// two substitution data: a substitution shifts, conses a term onto another"
600..676 Comment "// or lifts one under a binder, and a renaming shifts or lifts. Lifting is a"
677..748 Comment "// constructor, so the substitution laws reach their inductive steps by"
749..813 Comment "// conversion; lifting written as a definition reaches them too."
814..816 Comment "//"
817..892 Comment "// The argument, file by file: this base; the laws that hold by computation"
893..969 Comment "// (`sub-q-single`, `sub-q-lift`, `sub-lam`, `sub-app`); the congruences and"
970..1043 Comment "// the lemmas laws 3 and 4 are proved from (`congruence`, `shift-lookup`,"
1044..1111 Comment "// `rename-rename`, `lookup-weaken`, `subst-rename`, `subst-subst`,"
1112..1181 Comment "// `lift-as-definition`, `subst-id`, `subst-as-rename`); laws 3 and 4"
1182..1243 Comment "// (`sub-weaken-lift`, `sub-weaken-single`); the syntax model"
1244..1309 Comment "// (`syntax-model`) and the record of `LC`\'s models it packs into"
1310..1330 Comment "// (`model-record`)."
1332..1371 Comment "// The naturals, the de Bruijn indices."
1372..1378 Keyword "import"
1379..1380 StringLit "\""
1380..1404 StringLit "../model-in-source.gandr"
1404..1405 StringLit "\""
1405..1406 Other ";"
1408..1479 Comment "/// The single-substitution calculus of the pure λ-calculus: contexts,"
1480..1553 Comment "/// substitutions between them and terms in a context; the empty context,"
1554..1629 Comment "/// substitution, context extension, weakening, the newest variable, single"
1630..1696 Comment "/// substitution and lifting; abstraction and application; the six"
1697..1773 Comment "/// substitution laws. Its laws over the indexed sorts nest an operation the"
1774..1853 Comment "/// cell layer does not read there (#1510); `Model(LC)` derives from it all the"
1854..1863 Comment "/// same."
